      <p>Table visualization in the CLI provides viewing and flow search capabilities.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>Install the Network Observability CLI (<code>oc netobserv</code>) plugin.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Capture flows with filters enabled by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc netobserv flows --enable_filter=true --action=Accept --cidr=0.0.0.0/0 --protocol=TCP --port=49051"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Add filters to the <code>live table filter</code> prompt in the terminal to further refine the incoming flows. For example:
      <CodeBlock code={"live table filter: [SrcK8S_Zone:us-west-1b] press enter to match multiple regular expressions at once"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>Use the <strong>PageUp</strong> and <strong>PageDown</strong> keys to toggle between <strong>None</strong>, <strong>Resource</strong>, <strong>Zone</strong>, <strong>Host</strong>, <strong>Owner</strong> and <strong>all of the above</strong>.</li>
      <li>To stop capturing, press <Fragment set:html={"<kbd>"} />Ctrl+C<Fragment set:html={"</kbd>"} />. The data that was captured is written to two separate files in an <code>./output</code> directory located in the same path used to install the CLI.</li>
